WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.900
All right, let's get into audience questions
for the week, very relevant and prescient

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.900
questions today.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:12.730
The first is, hey, David could so call the
rhino's be better allies for removing Trump

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:19.830
than the never Biden people in November of
twenty twenty rhinos are Republicans in name

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.100
only.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.370
OK.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.160
I think that thinking that is sort of defeatist.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.369
And I'm going to tell you why.

00:00:26.369 --> 00:00:31.630
There is no doubt that there is a Republican
movement that hates Trump and wants to remove

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.630
him.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:36.530
This includes people like George Conway, the
husband of Trump adviser Kellyanne Conway.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:43.880
This includes people like, you know, there's
this Steve Schmidt is an adviser and Rick

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.829
Wilson, who I've interviewed on the show.

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:51.430
These are Republican strategist types who
don't like Trump and want to see him removed.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:55.880
Now, the question about allies could be interpreted
two ways.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.899
Number one is just like in the sheer numbers
of it, do I think there will be more Republicans

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.990
who abandoned Trump and vote Biden than the
number of never Biden people who would normally

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:09.500
be Democratic voters, but are going to either
not vote or vote third party or vote for Donald

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.730
Trump?

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.730
I think the answer is no.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.790
I mean, listen, every every election there
is abandonment.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:20.850
If you look at 2008, there were a bunch of
people who voted for Hillary in the Democratic

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:25.080
primary and then voted for John McCain in
2016.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:31.689
You saw some Bernie primary voters who abandoned
Hillary, who abandoned the party, so to speak,

00:01:31.689 --> 00:01:32.979
and voted for Trump.

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:37.210
It was actually a smaller number than the
number that did the abandonment in 2008 and

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:38.630
went to McCain.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:42.510
Every election you have that I don't think
the number is actually going to be that big.

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:47.040
And I know that the never Biden movement is
very, very loud online.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.680
But you have to understand that there's a
lot of things that are very, very loud online.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:54.570
And it turns out that they don't really reflect
reality as closely as we might imagine or

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:59.810
we might even hope the Bernie run is an example
of that.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.189
So much online activity.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:07.730
And then Bernie lost three consecutive Super
Tuesdays, only the last of.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:12.329
By that I mean the three Tuesdays in March
that have a bunch of elections.

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:16.889
Only the last one was even moderately affected
by the Corona virus.

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:21.150
And there's no particular reason to believe
that that actually hurt Bernie more than it

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.230
hurt Biden.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:29.409
So I don't actually think that the never Biden
movement is going to be what prevents Biden

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:31.049
from winning.

00:02:31.049 --> 00:02:35.439
I think that there is no question, though,
that we should welcome Republicans who are

00:02:35.439 --> 00:02:40.500
not going to vote Trump once Trump's out,
whoever the next president is, either Biden

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.790
in in winning in November or some other Democrat
winning four years from now.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:51.379
At some point, those Republicans are going
to be back to disagreeing with us on most

00:02:51.379 --> 00:02:52.379
policy.

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:53.379
And that's it.

00:02:53.379 --> 00:02:59.530
So the idea of them being allies, anybody
who doesn't vote for Trump votes for Biden.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.530
Right.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.379
Any one of those votes helps remove Donald
Trump and we'll take it.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:04.379
And we love it.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:05.379
And it's all fantastic.

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:09.419
The more people that realize that this guy
is a lethal menace, the better and more efficiently

00:03:09.419 --> 00:03:10.419
that we can remove him.

00:03:10.419 --> 00:03:17.469
But I worry about the hostility of saying,
man, some of these Republicans are better

00:03:17.469 --> 00:03:19.779
allies than the never Biden people.

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:21.079
We it's not one or the other.

00:03:21.079 --> 00:03:22.099
We need everybody.

00:03:22.099 --> 00:03:28.609
And there are reasons why people might be
Republicans and not want Trump.

00:03:28.609 --> 00:03:32.180
That would be completely unaligned with our
values.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:35.549
We might be not really a small government
conservative.

00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:36.909
They hate that he did the stimulus.

00:03:36.909 --> 00:03:40.779
Like there's people that are mad at Trump
on the right because he did the corona virus

00:03:40.779 --> 00:03:43.359
stimulus coronavirus stimulus wasn't big enough.

00:03:43.359 --> 00:03:47.150
I mean, OK, if they don't want to vote Trump
in November because of it and they're going

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:49.029
to help Biden win by one vote each.

00:03:49.029 --> 00:03:50.299
I'll take it.

00:03:50.299 --> 00:03:55.219
But the reason they disagree with Trump might
be completely not in line with our values.

00:03:55.219 --> 00:03:58.199
So everybody's an ally who helps remove Trump.

00:03:58.199 --> 00:04:02.069
But the idea that we want to start shaming
never Biden people by saying these rhinos

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:03.919
are even better allies for us.

00:04:03.919 --> 00:04:04.979
I don't think it's a good idea.

00:04:04.979 --> 00:04:05.979
I don't think it's pragmatic.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:17.069
I don't think it's based

00:04:17.069 --> 00:05:10.090
on

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:17.360
the facts either.

